        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-16T14:40:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Generally speaking most of our timing code uses SystemClock.elapsedRealtime() or elapsedRealtimeNanos. That has the advantage of never stepping due to clock changes. (And also it counts time spent in sleep, but currentTimeMillis does that as well.)\n\nI think currentTimeMillis is correct here unless the time steps during the test (unlikely unless the test runs soon after device boot when the NTP client starts). But you might also want to get into the habit of using elapsedRealtime everywhere.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 192,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 192,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "revId": "5243c1d3f47f2f9d6caa00fa26cded2dd96951d9",
