        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-16T14:40:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This should be a function parameter. Even though you (currently) only ever use 15000, letting the caller pass it that 15000 will make the calling code more readable.\n\nAlso - could we make this number lower? Waiting 15s for a test to run is not great, especially if someone is trying to debug failures.\n\nThat said, maybe we want to tune this once the test is in presubmit. We\u0027ve seen in the past that the test infrastructure can often be slow such that simple operations take a few seonds.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 264,
        "startChar": 35,
        "endLine": 264,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "5243c1d3f47f2f9d6caa00fa26cded2dd96951d9",
