      "lineNbr": 283,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-16T14:40:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think some waiting is probably necessary here, because after the setIngress... call returns, the settings observer needs to fire, and the connectivityservice handler thread has to process the event. That probably takes a millisecond or two even if there is nothing else going on. If this takes too long it will probably skew the results.\n\n500ms is a bit long though... is there something we can do to find out if the filter is installed? For example, do something something like run \"tc filter show dev testtap3\" once every few milliseconds until we see that the filter is installed? You could put that into a \"private void awaitFilterInstalled(String iface, int timeoutMs)\" method.\n\nCTS does have permission to run shell commands - see for example\n\nhttps://source.corp.google.com/aosp-master/packages/modules/Connectivity/tests/cts/net/src/android/net/cts/NetworkStatsManagerTest.java;l\u003d245\n\n- but of course it may not have permission to dump tc parameters.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 283,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 283,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "5243c1d3f47f2f9d6caa00fa26cded2dd96951d9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
